+### Word timestamps
+
+Fish Audio Drama 3 (`fish_omni`) can time words with no forced aligner, no
+ASR and no second model: a few heads of its full-attention layers read the
+text in order while it speaks, and stage 0 captures their attention logits
+over the request's text for every codec frame (one frame per decode step,
+44100 / 2048 = 21.53 Hz, so the resolution is 46.44 ms). Enable the capture on
+stage 0 with `hf_overrides` `fish_omni_word_timestamps: true` (the packaged
+overlay `vllm_omni/deploy/fish_omni_word_timestamps.yaml` does this), then
+send `"word_timestamps": true`:
+
+- **SSE stream** (`stream=true`): after each `speech.audio.delta` whose frames
+  settled words, a `speech.alignment.delta` event lists the words whose state
+  changed, in text order. `final: true` words are settled and never change
+  again; `final: false` words are the ones being spoken, whose spans still
+  grow. A last `speech.alignment.delta` with every word `final` precedes
+  `speech.audio.done`; its last word carries `tail_silence_ms`, an estimate of
+  the trailing silence the last word's span absorbs (the model keeps reading
+  the last word until end of speech), from the utterance's own speaking rate.
+  Words are decoded after the audio chunk is sent, so first audio is not
+  delayed; a word settles about four frames (190 ms) after it ends.
+  Milliseconds are integers; `resolution_ms` is the frame length.
+- **Non-streaming**: the `X-Word-Timestamps` header, a JSON list of
+  `{word, start_ms, end_ms}` (the last with `tail_silence_ms`), as with the
+  forced aligner (4 KB cap, `X-Word-Timestamps-Omitted` beyond it).
+- `stream_format="audio"` has no room for the words and is rejected with
+  `word_timestamps=true`. The WebSocket `/v1/audio/speech/stream` path keeps
+  the forced-aligner implementation.
+
+Words are whitespace-delimited; a token shared by two words gives both the
+same span, and a word the attention never dwells on is interpolated between
+its neighbours. Texts of more than 512 tokens (`fish_omni_alignment_max_text`)
+get audio but no timestamps. Reading position comes from the model's own
+attention, so a boundary is typically within a frame or two of the audio; see
+the [Drama 3 recipe](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-omni/blob/main/recipes/fishaudio/Drama-3.md#word-timestamps)
+for the head set and its limits.
+
 ### Voices Endpoint
 
 ```text
